0 A row of flat-belt displays compares two-wheel, triangular and multi-wheel loops around small rims.
0 Name: RUBBER_BELT-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Willy Tschager
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: Narrow blue and brown belts run between pairs of wheels. Yellow and orange belts take longer routes around intermediate wheels; an isolated dark ring sits around a single rim.
0 // Rigid construction: Most routes use 3482 axle-hole rims, with a 30155 rim in the final sample. There is no shared chassis or complete shaft-retention structure.
0 // Build lesson: Plan wheel centres and supporting shafts as one layout before adding a belt. Different silhouettes can suggest a conveyor, compact drive or guide roller assembly.
0 // Reuse: The fourth legacy route produces a tangent warning in the current synthesizer. A rim that looks suitable is not automatically a mechanically compatible pulley.
0 // Study 1: The blue belt forms a simple narrow loop around two aligned rims.
0 SYNTH BEGIN RUBBER_BELT 1
0 SYNTH SHOW
